IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `maib-core`

-- Motor Accidents (Liabilities and Compensation) Act 1973 (Tas) and Regulations 2020 -- the MAIB scheduled benefits,
-- from the seat of the individual.
--
-- SEAT: the person who suffers personal injury resulting directly from a motor accident; and, after a death, the
-- dependants (death benefits), the personal representative (funeral benefits) and the family members (counselling
-- services benefits) of the person killed. They ask: "Is MAIB liable to pay me? Which disability allowance, at what
-- weekly rate, from and until when? What death and funeral benefits does my family get? What cap applies to my medical
-- and disability benefits? What must I do, and by when?" The rules are in maib-core.l4; this module builds the core's
-- records from plain answers and restates no rule. Its names are its own: none is defined in maib-seat-board.l4.
--
-- FIGURES: the Regulations' own (Sch 1). Adult average weekly earnings (ABS 6302.0) are inputs: the figure last
-- published before the accident (Pt 5), and the two figures of the Pt 3 funeral formula.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `MAIB scheduled benefits -- the injured person's questions, and the family's after a death`

§§ `Building the core's records from plain answers`

GIVEN `how a vehicle registered in Tasmania was involved` IS A `How the injury resulted from the vehicle`
      `how an interstate vehicle was involved`            IS A `How the injury resulted from the vehicle`
      `how any other vehicle was involved`                IS A `How the injury resulted from the vehicle`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Vehicle involved`
`my vehicles` `how a vehicle registered in Tasmania was involved` `how an interstate vehicle was involved` `how any other vehicle was involved` MEANS
    LIST
        `Vehicle involved` WITH
            `its registration`                IS `registered in this State`
            `how the injury resulted from it` IS `how a vehicle registered in Tasmania was involved`
        `Vehicle involved` WITH
            `its registration`                IS `an interstate motor vehicle`
            `how the injury resulted from it` IS `how an interstate vehicle was involved`
        `Vehicle involved` WITH
            `its registration`                IS `neither registered in this State nor an interstate motor vehicle`
            `how the injury resulted from it` IS `how any other vehicle was involved`

GIVEN `hours`     IS A NUMBER
      `indefinite` IS A BOOLEAN
      `within a year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `certified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `accepted`  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Daily care facts`
`my daily care facts` `hours` `indefinite` `within a year` `certified` `accepted` MEANS
    `Daily care facts` WITH
        `hours a day of daily care the person requires or is likely to require` IS `hours`
        `the daily care is required for an indefinite period`                    IS `indefinite`
        `the daily care commences not later than one year after the date of the accident` IS `within a year`
        `a court has certified that the person requires daily care`              IS `certified`
        `the person accepted a payment into court or offer of compromise made on the basis that the person requires daily care` IS `accepted`

-- The conviction under the Road Safety (Alcohol and Drugs) Act 1970, as a plain choice.
DECLARE `My alcohol or drug driving conviction` IS ONE OF
    `none`
    `section 6 (1): driving with a prescribed concentration of alcohol`
    `section 14 (1A)`
    `section 14 (2)`
    `section 14 (5)`

GIVEN `the conviction`    IS A `My alcohol or drug driving conviction`
      `the concentration` IS A NUMBER
      `no contribution`   IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Section 24 (4) facts`
`my s 24 (4) facts` `the conviction` `the concentration` `no contribution` MEANS
    `Section 24 (4) facts` WITH
        `the conviction` IS
            CONSIDER `the conviction`
            WHEN `none` THEN `no conviction under s 6 (1), 14 (1A), 14 (2) or 14 (5)`
            WHEN `section 6 (1): driving with a prescribed concentration of alcohol` THEN `a conviction under s 6 (1)` `the concentration`
            WHEN `section 14 (1A)` THEN `a conviction under s 14 (1A)`
            WHEN `section 14 (2)` THEN `a conviction under s 14 (2)`
            WHEN `section 14 (5)` THEN `a conviction under s 14 (5)`
        `the person has satisfied the Board that the alcohol did not contribute in any way to the accident` IS `no contribution`

-- Sch 1 Pt 5 cl 7 (1): which of its five cases applies, as a plain choice.
DECLARE `How I was working before the accident` IS ONE OF
    `continuously for the whole 12 months before the day of the accident`
    `continuously, for one week or more but less than 12 months, up to the day of the accident`
    `for less than one week before the accident`
    `on my way to start a new job for the first time`
    `not working at the time, but a job seeker under cl 3 (2) (c)`

GIVEN `the case`       IS A `How I was working before the accident`
      `earnings`       IS A NUMBER
      `began`          IS A DATE
      `comparable`     IS A NUMBER
      `weeks`          IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Earnings record`
`my earnings record` `the case` `earnings` `began` `comparable` `weeks` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the case`
    WHEN `continuously for the whole 12 months before the day of the accident` THEN
        `continuously engaged for the entire 12 months before the day of the accident` `earnings`
    WHEN `continuously, for one week or more but less than 12 months, up to the day of the accident` THEN
        `continuously engaged for one week or more but less than 12 months` `began` `earnings`
    WHEN `for less than one week before the accident` THEN `engaged for less than one week` `comparable`
    WHEN `on my way to start a new job for the first time` THEN `travelling to take up employment for the first time` `comparable`
    WHEN `not working at the time, but a job seeker under cl 3 (2) (c)` THEN `entitled as a job seeker under cl 3 (2) (c)` `earnings` `weeks`

GIVEN `working`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `travelling` IS A BOOLEAN
      `aged 15`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `weeks worked` IS A NUMBER
      `seeking`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `business`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `household` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Work at the time of the accident`
`my work` `working` `travelling` `aged 15` `weeks worked` `seeking` `business` `household` MEANS
    `Work at the time of the accident` WITH
        `engaged in employment or an occupation for remuneration or profit`  IS `working`
        `travelling directly from home to take up employment or an occupation at the end of the journey` IS `travelling`
        `at least 15 years old, or exempt from school, on the day of the accident` IS `aged 15`
        `weeks engaged in employment or an occupation in the 12 months before the day of the accident` IS `weeks worked`
        `actively seeking employment through all avenues reasonably available, or certified unfit for work by a medical practitioner` IS `seeking`
        `carrying on a business for profit`                                   IS `business`
        `normally carried out household duties`                               IS `household`

§§ `Am I covered? (ss 2 (5), 2B, 23, 24)`

@export Do I require daily care under the MAIB scheme (s 2 (5), s 27A)? This opens the Tasmanian benefits to an interstate resident (s 23 (2)), lifts the medical cap and opens counselling benefits for the family.
GIVEN `hours a day of daily care I need, or am likely to need` IS A NUMBER @desc Hours a day of treatment, therapy, nursing, assistance, supervision, rehabilitation or other care you need, or are likely to need, because of the injury
      `I need it for an indefinite period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you need that care for an indefinite period (no end in sight)
      `it started, or will start, within one year after the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the daily care began, or will begin, no later than one year after the date of the accident
      `a court has certified that I require daily care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court, giving judgment for your damages, certified that you require daily care (s 27A (2))
      `I accepted a payment into court or offer made on the basis that I require daily care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you accepted a payment into court or an offer of compromise that was made on the basis that you require daily care (s 27A (3))
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I require daily care` IF
    `the person requires daily care` (`my daily care facts` `hours a day of daily care I need, or am likely to need` `I need it for an indefinite period` `it started, or will start, within one year after the accident` `a court has certified that I require daily care` `I accepted a payment into court or offer made on the basis that I require daily care`)

@export Is MAIB (the Motor Accidents Insurance Board) liable to pay me scheduled benefits for this motor accident, and which ones (ss 2B, 23 and 24)? Asks where the accident happened, where you live, which vehicles were involved, whether it was reported to police, and the exclusions.
GIVEN `where the accident happened` IS A `Place` @desc Where the motor accident happened: in this State (Tasmania), in another State or a Territory of Australia, or outside the Commonwealth
      `where I ordinarily live` IS A `Place` @desc Where your ordinary place of residence is: in this State (Tasmania), in another State or a Territory, or outside the Commonwealth (s 2B)
      `how a Tasmanian-registered vehicle was involved` IS A `How the injury resulted from the vehicle` @desc How a motor vehicle registered in Tasmania (even if its registration was suspended) caused your injury: a collision with it or action taken to avoid one, it moving out of control, the driving of it, or none of those (no such vehicle)
      `how an interstate vehicle was involved` IS A `How the injury resulted from the vehicle` @desc How an interstate motor vehicle (one normally used by a resident of another State or a Territory there, and required to be registered there) caused your injury: a collision or avoiding one, out of control, the driving of it, or none of those
      `how any other vehicle was involved` IS A `How the injury resulted from the vehicle` @desc How any other motor vehicle (unregistered, or registered overseas) caused your injury: a collision or avoiding one, out of control, the driving of it, or none of those
      `hours a day of daily care I need` IS A NUMBER @desc Hours a day of daily care (treatment, nursing, assistance, supervision, rehabilitation) you need or are likely to need because of the injury; 0 if none
      `I need daily care indefinitely` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you need that daily care for an indefinite period
      `my daily care started within a year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the daily care began, or will begin, within one year after the accident
      `a court certified that I require daily care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court has certified that you require daily care (s 27A (2))
      `I accepted an offer on the basis that I require daily care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you accepted a payment into court or offer of compromise made on the basis that you require daily care (s 27A (3))
      `the accident was reported to police as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident was reported to a police officer (in the State or Territory where it happened) as soon as practicable
      `the Board has excused a late report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was not reported as soon as practicable, whether MAIB has decided to excuse that
      `I intentionally caused or tried to cause injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury results from you intentionally causing, or trying to cause, injury to yourself or someone else
      `workers compensation is payable for my injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether workers compensation (from an employer, under a law of Tasmania, the Commonwealth or another State or Territory) is payable for this injury
      `another motor accident scheme pays compensation for my injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether compensation is payable for this injury under a motor accidents compensation law of the Commonwealth or another State or Territory, or an insurance policy that law requires
      `it is an asbestos disease compensated under the 2011 Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury is an asbestos-related disease for which you are entitled to compensation under the Asbestos-Related Diseases (Occupational Exposure) Compensation Act 2011
      `it results from ionizing radiation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury results from your being subjected to ionizing radiation
      `I was taking part in a motor vehicle race` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident happened in a motor vehicle race in which you were taking part (competing, conducting it, or assisting)
      `the vehicle was used for a crime of dishonesty or violence I was party to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident resulted from using a vehicle in, or to further, an offence of dishonesty or violence, and you were a party to that use
      `a vehicle was being used for terrorism` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a motor vehicle in the accident was being used for an act of terrorism
      `I owned the vehicle whose use caused the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were the owner (or registered operator) of the motor vehicle whose use resulted in the accident
      `I drove the vehicle whose use caused the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were driving the motor vehicle whose use resulted in the accident
      `the accident resulted from the use of my vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident resulted from the use of the vehicle you owned or drove; FALSE if you were a passenger or pedestrian
      `the kind of my vehicle` IS A `Kind of vehicle` @desc The kind of vehicle you owned or drove: a trail bike, farm bike or beach buggy; a small trailer, towed agricultural implement or trailer towed by a working agricultural machine (reg 11 (2)); or any other motor vehicle
      `my vehicle is an interstate vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle you owned or drove is normally used, and required to be registered, in another State or a Territory
      `the MAIB premium for its use had been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tasmanian MAIB premium (s 30) for its use, in the circumstances and conditions in which it was being used, had been paid
      `an interstate premium is required for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an interstate vehicle, whether the law of its State or Territory requires a compulsory third-party premium or levy for its use
      `the interstate premium had been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an interstate vehicle, whether that interstate premium for its use in the circumstances had been paid
      `I knew or ought to have known the premium was unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you were the driver, whether you knew or ought to have known that the premium had not been paid
      `it was a permitted out-of-State vehicle with third party insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was a vehicle registered outside Tasmania that could lawfully be driven here unregistered, with a third party insurance policy in force (s 24 (1A))
      `my conviction arising out of my driving` IS A `Section 24 (2) (a) conviction` @desc Any conviction arising out of your driving at the time of the accident: manslaughter, causing death or grievous bodily harm by dangerous driving, dangerous driving, Traffic Act s 32 (1), Road Safety (Alcohol and Drugs) Act s 4, a similar interstate offence, or none
      `I was driving` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were driving a motor vehicle at the time of the accident
      `I held a licence of the relevant class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you held a driver licence of the class for that vehicle
      `I was exempt or otherwise authorised to drive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were exempt from holding such a licence or otherwise authorised to drive that class of vehicle
      `my licence lapsed only by inadvertence and could be renewed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an earlier licence was not renewed only because you forgot to apply, it can still be renewed, and there is no reason to think it would not be (s 24 (3))
      `my licence was suspended only for unpaid fines` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your licence was suspended under s 55 of the Monetary Penalties Enforcement Act 2005 (or an interstate equivalent), and you were otherwise driving lawfully (s 24 (3A))
GIVETH A `The Board's liability`
DECIDE `Is MAIB liable to pay me scheduled benefits for this accident` IS
    `the Board's liability for each scheduled benefit` `the accident` `the s 24 (1) facts` `the s 24 (2) facts`
    WHERE
        `the accident` MEANS
            `Accident facts` WITH
                -- The date is not read by ss 23-24; a fixed placeholder.
                `date of the motor accident`                       IS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2026
                `where the motor accident occurred`                IS `where the accident happened`
                `the injured person's ordinary place of residence` IS `where I ordinarily live`
                `the vehicles involved`                            IS `my vehicles` `how a Tasmanian-registered vehicle was involved` `how an interstate vehicle was involved` `how any other vehicle was involved`
                `the daily care facts`                             IS `my daily care facts` `hours a day of daily care I need` `I need daily care indefinitely` `my daily care started within a year` `a court certified that I require daily care` `I accepted an offer on the basis that I require daily care`
                `the accident was reported to a police officer as soon as practicable` IS `the accident was reported to police as soon as practicable`
                `the Board has determined that the failure to report should be excused` IS `the Board has excused a late report`
        `the s 24 (1) facts` MEANS
            `Section 24 (1) facts` WITH
                `the injury results from the person intentionally causing or attempting to cause personal injury to themself or another` IS `I intentionally caused or tried to cause injury`
                `compensation is payable for the injury under a workers compensation law of this State, the Commonwealth or another State or Territory` IS `workers compensation is payable for my injury`
                `compensation is payable for the injury under a motor accidents compensation law of the Commonwealth or another State or Territory, or a policy it requires` IS `another motor accident scheme pays compensation for my injury`
                `an asbestos-related disease for which the person is entitled to compensation under the Asbestos-Related Diseases (Occupational Exposure) Compensation Act 2011` IS `it is an asbestos disease compensated under the 2011 Act`
                `the injury results from the person being subjected to ionizing radiation` IS `it results from ionizing radiation`
                `the accident occurred in a motor vehicle race in which the person was taking part` IS `I was taking part in a motor vehicle race`
                `the vehicle was used in or in furtherance of an offence of dishonesty or violence, the person being a party to that use` IS `the vehicle was used for a crime of dishonesty or violence I was party to`
                `a motor vehicle in the accident was being used for an act of terrorism` IS `a vehicle was being used for terrorism`
                `the person's own vehicle` IS
                    `The person's own vehicle` WITH
                        `the person was its owner`                                   IS `I owned the vehicle whose use caused the accident`
                        `the person was its driver`                                  IS `I drove the vehicle whose use caused the accident`
                        `the motor accident results from its use`                    IS `the accident resulted from the use of my vehicle`
                        `its kind`                                                   IS `the kind of my vehicle`
                        `it is an interstate motor vehicle`                          IS `my vehicle is an interstate vehicle`
                        `a premium for its use in the circumstances had been paid`   IS `the MAIB premium for its use had been paid`
                        `an interstate premium is required for it`                   IS `an interstate premium is required for it`
                        `an interstate premium for its use in the circumstances had been paid` IS `the interstate premium had been paid`
                        `the driver knew or ought to have known that the premium had not been paid` IS `I knew or ought to have known the premium was unpaid`
                        `it was a permitted out-of-State vehicle with a third party insurance policy in force` IS `it was a permitted out-of-State vehicle with third party insurance`
        `the s 24 (2) facts` MEANS
            `Section 24 (2) facts` WITH
                `conviction arising out of the person's driving at the time of the accident` IS `my conviction arising out of my driving`
                `the person was driving a motor vehicle at the time of the accident`       IS `I was driving`
                `the person held a driver licence of the relevant class`                   IS `I held a licence of the relevant class`
                `the person was exempted from holding one, or otherwise authorised to drive a vehicle of that class` IS `I was exempt or otherwise authorised to drive`
                `s 24 (3): an earlier licence was not renewed by inadvertence and could be renewed` IS `my licence lapsed only by inadvertence and could be renewed`
                `s 24 (3A): the licence was suspended only for unpaid monetary penalties` IS `my licence was suspended only for unpaid fines`

§§ `Claiming (s 23 (2A), reg 10, s 28)`

@export What must I do to claim MAIB scheduled benefits, and by when: report to police, give MAIB written notice of the injury, and bring the claim (s 23 (2A), reg 10 (2)-(4))?
GIVEN `the date of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date of the death, loss or care` IS A DATE @desc The date the claim runs from: the date of the death, the date the loss or expense was incurred, or the date the gratuitous care was provided (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `I have reported the accident to police` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident has been reported to a police officer
      `the Tribunal extended the notice period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tasmanian Civil and Administrative Tribunal has extended the period for written notice (reg 10 (3)-(4))
      `the notice period was extended to` IS A DATE @desc If so, the date to which the Tribunal extended it; otherwise any date (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the Tribunal extended the claim period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has extended the period for bringing the claim
      `the claim period was extended to` IS A DATE @desc If so, the date to which the Tribunal extended it; otherwise any date (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A `Steps to claim`
DECIDE `What must I do to claim, and by when` IS
    `the steps to claim` `I have reported the accident to police`
        (`the last day for written notice of the injury` `the date of the accident` `the Tribunal extended the notice period` `the notice period was extended to`)
        (`the last day to bring the claim` `the date of the death, loss or care` `the Tribunal extended the claim period` `the claim period was extended to`)

@export Was my written notice of the injury given, and my claim brought, in time (reg 10 (2)-(4))?
GIVEN `the date of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date I gave MAIB written notice of the injury` IS A DATE @desc The date written notice of the injury was given to MAIB (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date of the death, loss or care` IS A DATE @desc The date of the death, the date the loss or expense was incurred, or the date the gratuitous care was provided (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date I brought the claim` IS A DATE @desc The date the claim was made to MAIB (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the Tribunal extended the notice period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has extended the period for written notice
      `the notice period was extended to` IS A DATE @desc If so, the date to which it was extended; otherwise any date (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the Tribunal extended the claim period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has extended the period for bringing the claim
      `the claim period was extended to` IS A DATE @desc If so, the date to which it was extended; otherwise any date (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A `Claim timing`
DECIDE `Is my claim in time` IS
    `the reg 10 (2) timing of` `the date I gave MAIB written notice of the injury`
        (`the last day for written notice of the injury` `the date of the accident` `the Tribunal extended the notice period` `the notice period was extended to`)
        `the date I brought the claim`
        (`the last day to bring the claim` `the date of the death, loss or care` `the Tribunal extended the claim period` `the claim period was extended to`)

@export Can I take MAIB's decision on my claim to the Tasmanian Civil and Administrative Tribunal (s 28 (2))?
GIVEN `I disagree with MAIB's determination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are aggrieved by MAIB's determination of whether you are covered, your right to a benefit, or its amount
      `MAIB has refused or failed to pay me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether MAIB has refused, or failed, to pay you a scheduled benefit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I take MAIB's decision to the Tribunal` IF
    `the person may refer the matter to the Tribunal under s 28 (2)` `I disagree with MAIB's determination` `MAIB has refused or failed to pay me`

@export Does a Commonwealth pension I receive reduce my MAIB scheduled benefits (s 26)?
GIVEN `I receive or am entitled to a Commonwealth pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive, or are entitled to, a Commonwealth pension (a periodical payment for age, disability or a death, such as the Age Pension or Disability Support Pension)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my Commonwealth pension reduce my MAIB benefits` IF
    `I receive or am entitled to a Commonwealth pension` AND `the 2020 Regulations reduce a scheduled benefit for a Commonwealth pension (s 26)`

§§ `Medical benefits and the cap (Sch 1 Pt 1 cl 8, Pt 2)`

@export What cap applies to my MAIB medical and disability benefits for this accident (Sch 1 Pt 1 cl 8)? Disability allowances (weekly payments) do not count towards it.
GIVEN `the date of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `hours a day of daily care I need` IS A NUMBER @desc Hours a day of daily care you need or are likely to need because of the injury; 0 if none
      `I need daily care indefinitely` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you need that daily care for an indefinite period
      `my daily care started within a year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the daily care began, or will begin, within one year after the accident
      `a court certified that I require daily care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court has certified that you require daily care (s 27A (2))
      `I accepted an offer on the basis that I require daily care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you accepted a payment into court or offer of compromise made on the basis that you require daily care (s 27A (3))
      `days I was a hospital in-patient continuously from the accident` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days you were a hospital in-patient without a break, starting on the day of the accident; 0 if none
GIVETH A `Cap answer`
DECIDE `What cap applies to my medical and disability benefits` IS
    `the cl 8 limit for` `the date of the accident`
        (`the person requires daily care` (`my daily care facts` `hours a day of daily care I need` `I need daily care indefinitely` `my daily care started within a year` `a court certified that I require daily care` `I accepted an offer on the basis that I require daily care`))
        `days I was a hospital in-patient continuously from the accident`

@export How much of this new medical or disability expense can MAIB still pay under the cl 8 cap, given what it has already paid (Sch 1 Pt 1 cl 8)?
GIVEN `the date of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `I require daily care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you require daily care (see the daily care question); if so there is no cap
      `days I was a hospital in-patient continuously from the accident` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days you were a hospital in-patient without a break, starting on the day of the accident
      `medical and disability benefits already paid` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars MAIB has already paid as medical benefits and disability benefits for this accident (not counting weekly disability allowances)
      `the new amount` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars of the new medical or disability benefit that would otherwise be payable
GIVETH A `MAIB amount`
DECIDE `How much more can MAIB pay under the cap` IS
    `the part payable under the cap` (`the cl 8 limit for` `the date of the accident` `I require daily care` `days I was a hospital in-patient continuously from the accident`) `medical and disability benefits already paid` `the new amount`

@export How much of this treatment or travel expense will MAIB pay as medical benefits (Sch 1 Pt 2)? Assumes MAIB is liable under ss 23-24; the cl 8 cap is a separate question.
GIVEN `the date of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident, the date you were injured (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `what the expense is for` IS A `Kind of treatment` @desc What the expense is for: travel by taxi to treatment, travel by any other means to treatment, or other treatment (medical, surgical, dental, psychological, physiotherapy, hospital, ambulance, nursing, rehabilitation, medicines, aids)
      `the amount I paid or owe` IS A NUMBER @desc The expense incurred, in dollars
      `the cost in the most economical practicable way` IS A NUMBER @desc What the treatment would have cost if provided in the most economical manner practicable in the circumstances; if no cheaper way, the same amount
      `the treatment is warranted, beneficial and curative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the treatment is warranted, beneficial to you and curative of your injury (MAIB's view, or the Tribunal's)
      `the treatment was within Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the treatment was required, and obtained, within the Commonwealth (Australia)
      `Medicare or other Commonwealth amounts for it` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars paid, or required to be paid, for this treatment under a Commonwealth law, such as Medicare benefits; 0 if none
      `the travel is to a provider MAIB has approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For travel, whether it is to treatment from a person MAIB has determined; for other treatment any answer
      `the one-way distance in kilometres` IS A NUMBER @desc For travel, the one-way distance in kilometres; for other treatment 0
      `the date of the travel` IS A DATE @desc For travel, the date of the trip; for other treatment any date (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `a doctor certified I need a taxi` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a taxi, whether a medical practitioner has certified that, because of the injury, you require a taxi to travel
      `I require daily care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you require daily care (see the daily care question)
GIVETH A `MAIB amount`
DECIDE `How much of this expense will MAIB pay as medical benefits` IS
    `the medical benefit for` `the expense` `the date of the accident` `I require daily care`
    WHERE
        `the expense` MEANS
            `Treatment expense` WITH
                `kind of treatment`                                              IS `what the expense is for`
                `the expense incurred`                                           IS `the amount I paid or owe`
                `the expense if provided in the most economical manner practicable` IS `the cost in the most economical practicable way`
                `the treatment is warranted, beneficial and curative`            IS `the treatment is warranted, beneficial and curative`
                `the treatment is required within the Commonwealth`              IS `the treatment was within Australia`
                `sums paid or payable for it under a law of the Commonwealth`    IS `Medicare or other Commonwealth amounts for it`
                `the travel is to treatment from a person determined by the Board` IS `the travel is to a provider MAIB has approved`
                `the one-way distance travelled in kilometres`                   IS `the one-way distance in kilometres`
                `the date of the travel`                                         IS `the date of the travel`
                `a medical practitioner certifies that the person requires a taxi because of the injury` IS `a doctor certified I need a taxi`

§§ `Disability allowances (Sch 1 Pt 5) -- for an injured person who cannot work or keep house`

@export Which MAIB disability allowances could apply to me: the employed person's allowance, the self-employed person's replacement allowance, the housekeeping allowance (Sch 1 Pt 5 cl 2-5)?
GIVEN `I was working for pay or profit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the time of the accident, you were working in a job or occupation for pay or profit (including while on leave or stood down, or holding an office of profit)
      `I was on my way from home to start work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were travelling directly from home to the place where you were to start work at the end of that journey
      `I was at least 15 or exempt from school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the day of the accident, you were at least 15 years old or exempt from attending school
      `weeks I worked in the 12 months before` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks in total you worked for pay or profit in the 12 months before the day of the accident
      `I was looking for work or certified unfit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were actively seeking work through all avenues reasonably available, or certified by a doctor as unfit for work through injury or illness
      `I was carrying on a business for profit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were carrying on a business, profession or trade for profit (not as an employee)
      `I normally did household duties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you normally carried out household duties at the time of the accident
GIVETH A `Allowances that may apply`
DECIDE `Which disability allowances could apply to me` IS
    `the disability allowances that may apply for` (`my work` `I was working for pay or profit` `I was on my way from home to start work` `I was at least 15 or exempt from school` `weeks I worked in the 12 months before` `I was looking for work or certified unfit` `I was carrying on a business for profit` `I normally did household duties`)

@export What are my average weekly earnings for the MAIB employed person's allowance (Sch 1 Pt 5 cl 7)?
GIVEN `the date of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `how I was working before the accident` IS A `How I was working before the accident` @desc Which case applies: continuously for the whole 12 months before; continuously for a week or more but under 12 months; for less than a week; on the way to start a new job for the first time; or a job seeker under cl 3 (2) (c)
      `my earnings in that period` IS A NUMBER @desc Your earnings (pay and business profits, not counting your employer's compulsory superannuation contributions) over the 12 months, or since your continuous work began, or (job seeker) in the weeks you had earnings in the 12 months before
      `the day my continuous work began` IS A DATE @desc If you had worked continuously for less than 12 months, the day that work began; otherwise any date (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the average weekly earnings of someone in the same work` IS A NUMBER @desc If you had worked less than a week, or were starting a new job, the average weekly earnings of a person in the same (or the closest) employment; otherwise 0
      `the number of weeks I had earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc For a job seeker, the number of weeks in the 12 months before the accident in which you had earnings; otherwise 0
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my average weekly earnings` IS
    `the average weekly earnings under cl 7` `the date of the accident` (`my earnings record` `how I was working before the accident` `my earnings in that period` `the day my continuous work began` `the average weekly earnings of someone in the same work` `the number of weeks I had earnings`)

@export What is my MAIB employed person's allowance: the weekly rate, this week's amount, and from and until when it can be paid (Sch 1 Pt 5 cl 3, 6, 7; s 24 (4))? Assumes MAIB is liable under ss 23-24.
GIVEN `the date of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `I was working for pay or profit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the time of the accident, you were working in a job or occupation for pay or profit (including while on leave or stood down)
      `I was on my way from home to start work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were travelling directly from home to the place where you were to start work
      `I was at least 15 or exempt from school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the day of the accident, you were at least 15 or exempt from attending school
      `weeks I worked in the 12 months before` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks in total you worked for pay or profit in the 12 months before the day of the accident
      `I was looking for work or certified unfit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were actively seeking work through all avenues reasonably available, or certified by a doctor as unfit for work
      `how I was working before the accident` IS A `How I was working before the accident` @desc Which cl 7 case applies to your earnings (see the average weekly earnings question)
      `my earnings in that period` IS A NUMBER @desc Your earnings over that period, not counting your employer's compulsory superannuation contributions
      `the day my continuous work began` IS A DATE @desc If you had worked continuously for less than 12 months, the day that work began; otherwise any date (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the average weekly earnings of someone in the same work` IS A NUMBER @desc If you had worked less than a week, or were starting a new job, the average weekly earnings of a person in the same work; otherwise 0
      `the number of weeks I had earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc For a job seeker, the number of weeks in the 12 months before with earnings; otherwise 0
      `adult average weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The ABS adult average weekly earnings (full-time adult ordinary time earnings, catalogue 6302.0) last published before the accident, in dollars
      `I was wholly unable to do my usual work within 20 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, within the 20 days starting on the day of the accident, the injury left you wholly unable to do your usual job or occupation
      `what I earned from work this week` IS A NUMBER @desc Pay or profit you received from any work for the week asked about; 0 if none
      `my alcohol or drug driving conviction` IS A `My alcohol or drug driving conviction` @desc Any conviction, for your driving of a vehicle in the accident, under s 6 (1), 14 (1A), 14 (2) or 14 (5) of the Road Safety (Alcohol and Drugs) Act 1970, or none
      `my alcohol concentration` IS A NUMBER @desc For a s 6 (1) conviction, the concentration of alcohol (grams per 210 litres of breath or per 100 millilitres of blood); otherwise 0
      `I satisfied MAIB the alcohol did not contribute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a s 6 (1) conviction, whether you have satisfied MAIB that the alcohol did not contribute in any way to the accident
GIVETH AN `Allowance answer`
DECIDE `What is my employed person's allowance` IS
    `the employed person's allowance for` `the date of the accident`
        (`my work` `I was working for pay or profit` `I was on my way from home to start work` `I was at least 15 or exempt from school` `weeks I worked in the 12 months before` `I was looking for work or certified unfit` FALSE FALSE)
        (`the average weekly earnings under cl 7` `the date of the accident` (`my earnings record` `how I was working before the accident` `my earnings in that period` `the day my continuous work began` `the average weekly earnings of someone in the same work` `the number of weeks I had earnings`))
        `adult average weekly earnings`
        `I was wholly unable to do my usual work within 20 days`
        `what I earned from work this week`
        (`my s 24 (4) facts` `my alcohol or drug driving conviction` `my alcohol concentration` `I satisfied MAIB the alcohol did not contribute`)
    -- The business and household fields of `my work` are not read by cl 3; fixed placeholders (FALSE).

@export What is my MAIB self-employed person's replacement allowance: the weekly rate, and from and until when (Sch 1 Pt 5 cl 4, 6; s 24 (4))? Assumes MAIB is liable under ss 23-24.
GIVEN `the date of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `I was carrying on a business for profit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the time of the accident, you were carrying on a business, profession or trade for profit (not as an employee)
      `someone is paid to run my business while I am disabled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, so that the business keeps going while you are disabled, arrangements have been made for another person to be paid to conduct it
      `what I pay that person a week` IS A NUMBER @desc The remuneration, gratuity or reward paid each week to the person conducting your business, in dollars
      `adult average weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The ABS adult average weekly earnings last published before the accident, in dollars
      `the value of the hours I work in the business a week` IS A NUMBER @desc If you have gone back to the business in a reduced capacity, the weekly value of your hours as MAIB determines it; otherwise 0
      `I was wholly unable to run my business within 20 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, within the 20 days starting on the day of the accident, the injury left you wholly unable to conduct your business
      `my alcohol or drug driving conviction` IS A `My alcohol or drug driving conviction` @desc Any conviction for your driving in the accident under s 6 (1), 14 (1A), 14 (2) or 14 (5) of the Road Safety (Alcohol and Drugs) Act 1970, or none
      `my alcohol concentration` IS A NUMBER @desc For a s 6 (1) conviction, the concentration of alcohol; otherwise 0
      `I satisfied MAIB the alcohol did not contribute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a s 6 (1) conviction, whether you have satisfied MAIB that the alcohol did not contribute in any way to the accident
GIVETH AN `Allowance answer`
DECIDE `What is my self-employed person's replacement allowance` IS
    `the self-employed person's replacement allowance for` `the date of the accident`
        (`my work` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE `I was carrying on a business for profit` FALSE)
        `someone is paid to run my business while I am disabled`
        `what I pay that person a week`
        `adult average weekly earnings`
        `the value of the hours I work in the business a week`
        `I was wholly unable to run my business within 20 days`
        (`my s 24 (4) facts` `my alcohol or drug driving conviction` `my alcohol concentration` `I satisfied MAIB the alcohol did not contribute`)
    -- Only the business field of `my work` is read by cl 4; the others are fixed placeholders.

@export What is my MAIB housekeeping allowance: the weekly rate, and from and until when (Sch 1 Pt 5 cl 5, 6; s 24 (4))? Assumes MAIB is liable under ss 23-24.
GIVEN `the date of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `I normally did household duties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you normally carried out household duties at the time of the accident
      `the weekly cost of paying someone to do my usual household duties` IS A NUMBER @desc The reasonable commercial cost a week of engaging a person to do the household duties you normally did at least once a week before the accident, in dollars
      `the part of that a housekeeper I already employed was doing` IS A NUMBER @desc If you already employed a housekeeper before the injury, the weekly cost of the duties that housekeeper was already doing; otherwise 0
      `days I was a hospital in-patient continuously from the accident` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days you were a hospital in-patient without a break, starting on the day of the accident; 0 if none
      `I was wholly unable to do household duties within 20 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, within the 20 days starting on the day of the accident, the injury left you wholly unable to do ordinary household duties
      `my alcohol or drug driving conviction` IS A `My alcohol or drug driving conviction` @desc Any conviction for your driving in the accident under s 6 (1), 14 (1A), 14 (2) or 14 (5) of the Road Safety (Alcohol and Drugs) Act 1970, or none
      `my alcohol concentration` IS A NUMBER @desc For a s 6 (1) conviction, the concentration of alcohol; otherwise 0
      `I satisfied MAIB the alcohol did not contribute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a s 6 (1) conviction, whether you have satisfied MAIB that the alcohol did not contribute in any way to the accident
GIVETH AN `Allowance answer`
DECIDE `What is my housekeeping allowance` IS
    `the housekeeping allowance for` `the date of the accident`
        (`my work` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE `I normally did household duties`)
        `the weekly cost of paying someone to do my usual household duties`
        `the part of that a housekeeper I already employed was doing`
        `days I was a hospital in-patient continuously from the accident`
        `I was wholly unable to do household duties within 20 days`
        (`my s 24 (4) facts` `my alcohol or drug driving conviction` `my alcohol concentration` `I satisfied MAIB the alcohol did not contribute`)
    -- Only the household field of `my work` is read by cl 5; the others are fixed placeholders.

@export Can my MAIB disability allowance be paid for this day (Sch 1 Pt 5 cl 3 (4), 4 (3), 5 (2), 6 (1))? Not for the first 7 days, not while outside Australia, and only while wholly disabled as the period requires.
GIVEN `the date of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `which allowance` IS A `Disability allowance` @desc Which allowance: an employed person's allowance, a self-employed person's replacement allowance, or a housekeeping allowance
      `days I was a hospital in-patient continuously from the accident` IS A NUMBER @desc For the housekeeping allowance, how many days you were a hospital in-patient without a break from the day of the accident; otherwise 0
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day asked about (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `that day I was wholly unable to do my usual work, run my business, or do household duties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on that day, the injury left you wholly unable to do your usual work (employed), conduct your business with someone paid to run it (self-employed), or do your normal household duties (housekeeping)
      `that day I was wholly unable to do any work I am suited to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on that day, the injury left you wholly unable to do any work you would otherwise be reasonably suited to by education, training, experience or ability (after the first 104 weeks)
      `that day I was outside Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were outside the Commonwealth (Australia) on that day
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my disability allowance be paid for this day` IF
    `the allowance is payable on` `the periods` `the day` `that day I was wholly unable to do my usual work, run my business, or do household duties` `that day I was wholly unable to do any work I am suited to` `that day I was outside Australia`
    WHERE
        -- The rates are not read here; 0 is a fixed placeholder. The dates are the core's.
        `the periods` MEANS
            IF `which allowance` EQUALS `a housekeeping allowance`
            THEN `weekly allowance` `which allowance` 0 0 (`the first day a disability allowance can be paid` `the date of the accident`) (`the last day of the housekeeping period` `the date of the accident` `days I was a hospital in-patient continuously from the accident`) (`the last day of the housekeeping period` `the date of the accident` `days I was a hospital in-patient continuously from the accident`)
            ELSE `weekly allowance` `which allowance` 0 0 (`the first day a disability allowance can be paid` `the date of the accident`) (`the last day of the 104 weeks` `the date of the accident`) (`the last day of the prescribed period` `the date of the accident`)

@export What part of my MAIB disability allowance is still paid after my conviction for drink or drug driving in the accident (s 24 (4), (4A))?
GIVEN `my alcohol or drug driving conviction` IS A `My alcohol or drug driving conviction` @desc Your conviction, for your driving of a vehicle in the accident, under s 6 (1), 14 (1A), 14 (2) or 14 (5) of the Road Safety (Alcohol and Drugs) Act 1970, or none
      `my alcohol concentration` IS A NUMBER @desc For a s 6 (1) conviction, the concentration of alcohol (grams per 210 litres of breath or per 100 millilitres of blood); otherwise 0
      `I satisfied MAIB the alcohol did not contribute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a s 6 (1) conviction, whether you have satisfied MAIB that the alcohol did not contribute in any way to the accident
GIVETH A `Proportion answer`
DECIDE `What part of my disability allowance is still paid after my conviction` IS
    `the s 24 (4) proportion for` (`my s 24 (4) facts` `my alcohol or drug driving conviction` `my alcohol concentration` `I satisfied MAIB the alcohol did not contribute`)

§§ `Accidents in another State or a Territory (s 23 (1AA)) -- for a Tasmanian injured interstate`

@export For an accident in another State or a Territory, how much does MAIB pay once the benefits payable under that State's or Territory's law are taken off (s 23 (1AA))?
GIVEN `the MAIB benefit otherwise payable` IS A NUMBER @desc The scheduled benefit, in dollars, MAIB would pay for an accident in Tasmania
      `the benefits payable to me under that State's or Territory's law` IS A NUMBER @desc The benefits payable to you for this injury under the law of the State or Territory where the accident happened, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much does MAIB pay after the other State's benefits` IS
    `the s 23 (1AA) amount` `the MAIB benefit otherwise payable` `the benefits payable to me under that State's or Territory's law`

§§ `After a death (Sch 1 Pts 1, 3 and 4) -- for the family and personal representative of a person killed`

@export Am I a dependant of the person killed in the motor accident, for MAIB death benefits (Sch 1 Pt 1 cl 1, 2, 4-7)?
GIVEN `my relationship to the person who died` IS A `Relationship to the person who died` @desc Your relationship: their spouse or partner in a significant relationship; their child (or a child of their marriage or relationship); their parent; a person in a caring relationship with them; or someone else
      `my age on the day they died` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years on the day of the death
      `I would have been financially dependent on them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, but for the death, you would be wholly or partly dependent on them for financial support
      `I would have been dependent on them for care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, but for the death, you would be wholly or partly dependent on them for care other than financial support
      `I have a spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a spouse or partner yourself
      `I am a full-time student` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a full-time student
      `I lived with them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you ordinarily lived with them at the same premises
      `I was principally dependent on them financially` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were principally dependent on them for financial support
      `I am the parent of their dependent child who needed their care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a parent or step-parent of a dependent child of theirs who, but for the death, would be dependent on them for care
      `I was born from a pregnancy at the time of the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were born after the accident from a pregnancy existing at the time of it
      `I was alive 30 days after the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were living at the end of 30 days starting on the day of the death (or, if born after it, on the day of your birth)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a dependant of the person who died` IF
    `is a dependant` (`Survivor` WITH
        `relationship to the person who died` IS `my relationship to the person who died`
        `age in years on the day of the death` IS `my age on the day they died`
        `would, but for the death, be wholly or partly dependent on the person for financial support` IS `I would have been financially dependent on them`
        `would, but for the death, be wholly or partly dependent on the person for care other than financial support` IS `I would have been dependent on them for care`
        `has a spouse` IS `I have a spouse`
        `is a full-time student` IS `I am a full-time student`
        `ordinarily resided with the person at the same premises` IS `I lived with them`
        `was principally dependent on the person for financial support` IS `I was principally dependent on them financially`
        `is the parent or step-parent of a dependent child who would, but for the death, be dependent on the person for care` IS `I am the parent of their dependent child who needed their care`
        `was born from a pregnancy at the time of the accident` IS `I was born from a pregnancy at the time of the accident`
        `survived the person by the cl 7 period of 30 days` IS `I was alive 30 days after the death`)

@export What MAIB death benefit lump sum does the family of the person killed get (Sch 1 Pt 4)? Assumes MAIB is liable under ss 23-24. MAIB divides it between the dependants.
GIVEN `the date of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the death resulted directly from the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the death resulted directly from the motor accident
      `dependants who are not dependent children` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependants survived who are not dependent children (for example a dependent spouse, parent or carer)
      `dependent children under 9` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependent children under 9 years of age survived
      `dependent children aged 9 to 17` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependent children aged 9 to 17 survived
      `dependent children aged 18 to 24` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependent children aged 18 to 24 survived (full-time students)
      `disability allowance paid before the death` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars of MAIB disability allowance paid to the person before they died; 0 if none
GIVETH A `MAIB amount`
DECIDE `What death benefit does the family get` IS
    `the death benefit lump sum for` `the date of the accident` `the death resulted directly from the accident` `dependants who are not dependent children` `dependent children under 9` `dependent children aged 9 to 17` `dependent children aged 18 to 24` `disability allowance paid before the death`

@export What is the most MAIB pays as funeral benefits for this accident (Sch 1 Pt 3 cl 2)? $7 500 plus $7 500 times the percentage increase in adult average weekly earnings since May 2007.
GIVEN `the date of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `adult AWE released in May 2007` IS A NUMBER @desc The ABS adult average weekly earnings for the February 2007 quarter, released in May 2007, in dollars
      `the latest adult AWE for a period ending in May` IS A NUMBER @desc The most recently released ABS adult average weekly earnings for a period ending in May, in dollars
GIVETH A `MAIB amount`
DECIDE `What is the most MAIB pays for the funeral` IS
    `the funeral benefit limit for` `the date of the accident` `adult AWE released in May 2007` `the latest adult AWE for a period ending in May`

@export What MAIB funeral benefit is payable to the personal representative of the person killed (Sch 1 Pt 3)? Assumes MAIB is liable under ss 23-24.
GIVEN `the date of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the death resulted directly from the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the death resulted directly from the motor accident
      `the burial or cremation expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc Expenses reasonably incurred in the burial or cremation, in dollars
      `of which for a gravestone` IS A NUMBER @desc The part of those expenses for providing or erecting a gravestone, in dollars; 0 if none
      `adult AWE released in May 2007` IS A NUMBER @desc The ABS adult average weekly earnings released in May 2007, in dollars
      `the latest adult AWE for a period ending in May` IS A NUMBER @desc The most recently released ABS adult average weekly earnings for a period ending in May, in dollars
GIVETH A `MAIB amount`
DECIDE `What funeral benefit is payable` IS
    `the funeral benefits payable for` `the date of the accident` `the death resulted directly from the accident` `the burial or cremation expenses` `of which for a gravestone` `adult AWE released in May 2007` `the latest adult AWE for a period ending in May`

§§ `Counselling for family members (Sch 1 Pt 7) -- where the injured person needs daily care or has died`

@export What MAIB counselling services benefit can I get as a family member of a person who needs daily care, or was killed, after a motor accident (Sch 1 Pt 7; s 23 (8))?
GIVEN `the date of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the injured person requires daily care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person requires daily care (see the daily care question)
      `the injured person died as a result` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person died as a result of the injury
      `my relationship to the injured person` IS A `Family relationship` @desc Your relationship: spouse or partner in a significant relationship; child; parent; sibling; a relative or step-relative living with them; or another person
      `I need counselling because of the injury or death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, because of that injury or death, you require counselling
      `the counsellor is or is supervised by a registered psychologist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the counselling is provided by, or under the supervision of, a registered psychologist
      `my counselling expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc The counselling expenses reasonably incurred, in dollars
GIVETH A `MAIB amount`
DECIDE `What counselling benefit can I get` IS
    `the counselling services benefit for` `the date of the accident` `the injured person requires daily care` `the injured person died as a result` `my relationship to the injured person` `I need counselling because of the injury or death` `the counsellor is or is supervised by a registered psychologist` `my counselling expenses`

§§ `Damages and daily care (s 27A) -- for a person who requires daily care and has sued`

@export After my damages judgment or accepted settlement, does MAIB still pay medical or disability benefits for this item or service (s 27A (4)-(6))?
GIVEN `the court certified, or I accepted an offer on the basis, that I require daily care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court certified that you require daily care, or you accepted a payment into court or offer of compromise made on that basis
      `my damages or the accepted offer include the future cost of this item` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the damages awarded, or the payment or offer you accepted, include an allowance for the future cost of this item or service
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `After my damages, does MAIB still pay for this item` IF
    `s 27A: the Board pays medical or disability benefits for the item after the damages` `the court certified, or I accepted an offer on the basis, that I require daily care` `my damages or the accepted offer include the future cost of this item`
